# The item archive: 162 MB / 22,937 files of other newsrooms' article text and machine
# translations of it. Derived -- run.py's sync_archive() rebuilds every file from `items` -- and
# not ours to publish, so it never goes to a git host. See core/publish.py's PUBLIC note.
archive/*
# ...except the Commons lookup cache, which is our own 8 KB of licence/attribution metadata.
# Without it every cloud run re-queries Wikimedia for the same twelve entities.
!archive/images.json
# ...and the cited-article cache. Titles of other people's journalism this site has quoted; it has
# to outlive the items table, and a CI build needs it to render cards for articles that have since
# been deleted upstream. See core/reports_export.py's _load_cited().
!archive/cited.json

# Regenerated by every run from the database; committing them guarantees merge conflicts.
archive/hits.json
archive/reports.json
archive/pipeline.json

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.wrangler/
node_modules/
_site/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
